Z||000000||Harry||01-09-2000||12:00 PM||||It's come down to removing my tranny and replacing clutch/p.plate/t.o.b./and bushings on throw arm (yes pilot b. too)<BR>Ive seen many idea's on the best way to do this. What say's the Ogre?<BR>Do I drop just the tranny or the hole cradle?<BR>Ive done this job before just not on my Fiero. Please help.......||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||01-09-2000||12:14 PM||||I'm not Ogre but I'll put my nose in anyway.<BR>If you have a V6 I would suggest dropping the cradle and while doing the clutch modify your exhaust manifolds. Also neither my 85 GT nor 88 Formula has a pilot bearing (dealer has no listing for one)||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||01-09-2000||01:58 PM||||may as well drop the cradle. you can replace the cradle bushings and lower dog bone while its down.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Harry||01-09-2000||03:15 PM||||Phil,<BR>What do you mean by modify the manifolds?<BR>Ogre,<BR>Is there any associated problems with harness connections(the main) that I should be worried about?<BR>P.S. thanks||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||01-09-2000||03:47 PM||||If you have the V6 you can gain 6-8 HP(verified on dynos) by removing the restrictons inside total cost not counting time is the price of having them welded ($30)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Harry||01-09-2000||03:50 PM||||Cool I had no idea there was that much restriction, for stock (factory) headers they seem pretty cool.||||reg||7
Z||000006||theogre||01-09-2000||11:59 PM||||old electrical conectors can be delicate. Handle them carfully. expect at least one to break in some way. Usually you just snap off a latch, but they can be totaled if you aren't careful.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Harry||01-11-2000||10:17 PM||||I expected that, mines got 238K miles so I'm gonna be extra special careful in that department. Do they get Dialectric grease at the main connector?<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000008||theogre||01-11-2000||11:34 PM||||usually can't hurt any. especially if the weather packing is looking beat. go easy tho, SI grease doesn't compress. If you use too much it can make a mess or force the connector to work appart. all you need is a film on the metal parts to protect them.||||reg||1
